          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">What Is Root Canal Treatment?</h2>
          <p class="mt-3 text-base text-slate-700 leading-relaxed">
            Inside every tooth is a soft inner nerve tissue called the pulp. When deep decay, a crack, or a past injury allows bacteria to reach this nerve, it causes swelling and sharp pain. Root Canal Treatment (RCT) gently removes the infected pulp, cleans and shapes the tiny canals inside the tooth root, and seals them cleanly so the tooth stays in your mouth rather than needing removal.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] p-6 border border-slate-200">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Signs You May Need a Root Canal</h2>
          <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2.5 text-base text-slate-700 list-disc pl-5">
            <li>Continuous or throbbing toothache, especially while lying down at night.</li>
            <li>Pain when biting down or chewing food on one side.</li>
            <li>Lingering sensitivity to hot tea or cold water even after the drink is gone.</li>
            <li>Swelling in the nearby gum or a small pimple-like bump near the tooth root.</li>
            <li>A deeply decayed or darkened tooth noticed during a check-up.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div>
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Step-by-Step Procedure</h2>
          <div class="mt-4 rounded-2xl bg-[#F7F9FA] border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-12 items-center">
            <div class="sm:col-span-4 aspect-[4/3] overflow-hidden img-frame">
              <img src="/images/thumbs/digital-dental-xray-kishanpole-jaipur.webp" alt="In-house digital dental X-ray used before root canal treatment in Jaipur" loading="lazy" class="w-full h-full object-cover" width="640" height="480" referrerpolicy="no-referrer" />
            </div>
            <div class="sm:col-span-8 p-5">
              <span class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-wide text-[#2A9D8F]">In-House Digital Diagnostics</span>
              <h3 class="mt-1 text-lg font-bold text-[#1F2A30]">Instant X-Ray Clarity Before Starting</h3>
              <p class="mt-1.5 text-sm text-slate-600">We take a quick digital X-ray right on the chair so you can see the root length and infection depth clearly before your numbed RCT begins.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <ol class="mt-5 space-y-3 text-base text-slate-700 list-decimal pl-5">
            <li><strong>Digital X-Ray &amp; Numbing:</strong> Dr. Shubham Gupta takes a quick in-house digital dental X-ray to inspect the root shape and numbs the tooth thoroughly with local anaesthesia.</li>
            <li><strong>Cleaning the Canals:</strong> A small opening is made on top of the tooth to remove infected nerve tissue and disinfect the root canals gently.</li>
            <li><strong>Filling &amp; Sealing:</strong> Once the canal is clean and dry, it is sealed with biocompatible filling material to block future bacteria.</li>
            <li><strong>Final Restoration or Crown:</strong> A tooth-coloured filling closes the top, and a protective crown is advised when extra chewing strength is needed.</li>
          </ol>
        </div>

        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
